---
import Label from "../components/Label.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { ARCHIVE } from "../lib/archive";
import { CATEGORIES, REPO_URL, SECTION_ORDER, data } from "../lib/data";

const nf = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US");
const h2 = "mt-12 mb-3 border-t-2 border-ink pt-3 font-serif text-[1.7rem] font-extrabold leading-tight";
const a = "underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink";
---

<Base title="About" active="about" compact description="About the Sinhala News Corpus: an open, labelled dataset of Sinhala news headlines.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[44rem]">
    <Label si="මෙම පුවත්පත ගැන" en="About" />
    <h1 class="mt-1 font-serif text-[2.6rem] font-extrabold leading-[1.15] sm:text-[3.4rem]">
      පුවත්පතක් නොවේ. පුවත් දත්ත ගබඩාවකි.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 font-serif text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      Not a newspaper: an open dataset of Sinhala news headlines, laid out like one.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8] text-ink-2">
      <p class="first-letter:float-left first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:mt-1 first-letter:font-serif first-letter:text-[4.2rem] first-letter:font-extrabold first-letter:leading-[0.8] first-letter:text-accent">
        Sinhala is spoken by about seventeen million people, yet it is a low-resource language for computers. Clean, labelled
        Sinhala text is scarce, and much of what exists is broken by legacy fonts and invisible characters. The{" "}
        <a class={a} href={REPO_URL}>Sinhala News Corpus</a> collects news headlines every morning, cleans them carefully, and
        labels each one by topic, so that researchers can train and test Sinhala language models.
      </p>
      <p>
        මෙය සිංහල භාෂා තාක්ෂණ පර්යේෂණ සඳහා විවෘත දත්ත ව්‍යාපෘතියකි. සිරස්තලය, මුල් ලිපියට යොමුව, දිනය සහ මාතෘකාව පමණක් ගබඩා
        කෙරේ.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="my-10 border-y-2 border-ink py-6 text-center font-serif text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-snug sm:text-[1.9rem]">
      සිරස්තල සහ සබැඳි පමණි. ලිපි පිටපත් නොකෙරේ.
      <span class="mt-2 block font-sans text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-ink-3">Headlines and links only</span>
    </blockquote>

    <h2 class="mb-3 font-serif text-[1.7rem] font-extrabold leading-tight">How it works</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8] text-ink-2">
      Every day at 06:30 Sri Lanka time, a GitHub Actions job reads the public RSS feeds of {data.sources.length} news sites. Each
      headline is normalised (Unicode NFC), its zero-width joiners are kept only where they form letters like ශ්‍රී and ප්‍ර,
      legacy-font text is rejected, and duplicates are removed. The topic comes from the publisher's own section. The dataset holds{" "}
      <strong class="text-ink">{nf.format(data.total_all_time)}</strong> headlines so far; this site shows the last {data.days} days.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Publishers</h2>
    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
      <thead class="border-b border-ink font-sans text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-3">
        <tr><th class="py-2 font-medium">Publisher</th><th class="py-2 text-right font-medium">Headlines</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-rule">
        {
          data.sources.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2"><a class={a} href={s.homepage} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s.name}</a></td>
              <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-ink-2">{nf.format(s.count)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class={h2}>Sections</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8] text-ink-2">
      {[...SECTION_ORDER, "other" as const].map((c) => `${CATEGORIES[c].si} (${CATEGORIES[c].en})`).join(" · ")}
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Copyright and ethics</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-[1.8] text-ink-2 marker:text-accent">
      <li>Only the headline, link, date and topic are stored. Article text and news photographs are never copied, and article pages are never requested.</li>
      <li>The photographs on this site are public-domain archive pictures of Ceylon from around 1900. They illustrate sections, never individual stories, and every one is captioned as an archive photograph.</li>
      <li>Headlines remain the property of their publishers. Every headline links to the original article, so readers go to the publisher.</li>
      <li>robots.txt is checked before every request. Each site is read once a day at 06:30, with a backup check at 08:47 in case the first run is missed.</li>
      <li>Publishers who want their headlines removed can <a class={a} href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new`}>open an issue</a>; the source will be disabled and its rows removed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>Picture credits</h2>
    <p class="mb-3 leading-[1.8] text-ink-2">
      All photographs are in the public domain and were obtained through Wikimedia Commons. They are shown in greyscale with a
      printed halftone screen.
    </p>
    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      {
        ARCHIVE.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">{p.si}</span> — <span class="font-sans italic">{p.en}</span> ({p.year}). {p.credit}.{" "}
            <a class={a} href={p.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <h2 class={h2}>Use the data</h2>
    <p class="leading-[1.8] text-ink-2">
      Download the monthly CSV files from <a class={a} href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/data/raw`}>data/raw</a>, licensed
      <a class={a} href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/DATA_LICENSE.md`}>CC BY 4.0</a>. Counts per source and topic are in
      <a class={a} href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/STATS.md`}>STATS.md</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
